  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: 22 October 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    Nestyroo (nestyroo.com) is operated by AppricotAds LTD, a company registered in Bulgaria
    ("we", "us", "our"). This policy explains what personal information we collect through
    this website, why we collect it, and the choices you have. The site is intended for
    people in Australia.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Information you give us:</strong> your first name and email address when you sign up for deal alerts, and any optional interests you tick (for example baby and family, home savings, family travel or car costs). Interests are optional and help us send more relevant content.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> anything you send us through the contact form or by email.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> basic data such as IP address, browser type, device, pages visited and referring website, collected by our hosting provider and by standard server logs.</li>
    <li><strong>Cookies and similar technologies:</strong> we store a small item in your browser (local storage) to remember that you closed our sign-up pop-up. If we add analytics or advertising tools in future, we will update this policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not knowingly collect information from children. Our content is written for parents and carers.</p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send the deal alerts, guides and updates you signed up for.</li>
    <li>To tailor content to the interests you selected.</li>
    <li>To respond to your questions.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure, understand how it is used and improve it.</li>
    <li>To meet our legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We send marketing emails only with your consent, and every email includes an unsubscribe link.
    We comply with the Spam Act 2003 (Cth).
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information. We share it only with service providers that help us run the site, who may only use it for that purpose:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Our website hosting and form-handling provider (Netlify), which stores form submissions.</li>
    <li>Our code hosting provider (GitHub), which stores the website's files but not your sign-up details.</li>
    <li>An email service provider, once we start sending newsletters.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If we later offer partner offers (for example finance or insurance), we will ask for a separate,
    clearly named opt-in before sharing your details with that partner. We will not share your
    details with partners based on your newsletter sign-up alone.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you click one and buy, we may earn a commission
    at no extra cost to you. The retailer's own privacy policy applies once you leave our site. See our
    <a href="/legal/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Overseas storage</h2>
  <p>
    We are based in Bulgaria and our providers may store data in other countries, including the
    United States and the European Union. We take reasonable steps to make sure these providers
    protect your information.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your sign-up details until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them. We may keep a minimal
    record that you unsubscribed so we do not email you again. Contact messages are kept for as long as needed to respond.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reputable providers and reasonable technical measures to protect your information.
    No online service is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights and choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email or our <a href="/legal/unsubscribe/">unsubscribe page</a>.</li>
    <li>Ask to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because we are established in Bulgaria, the EU General Data Protection Regulation also applies to us,
    and you may have additional rights, including the right to complain to a data protection authority.
    If you are in Australia, you can also contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>

